name: sim.handleCollision
description: 
luaSynopsis: int collisionCount,int[2] collidingObjectHandles=sim.handleCollision(int collisionObjectHandle)
inputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. collisionObjectHandle: handle of the collision object or sim.handle_all or sim.handle_all_except_explicit. (sim.handle_all will handle all registered collision objects, while sim.handle_all_except_explicit will only handle those that are not marked as "explicit handling")
outputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. collisionCount: number of collisions.
2. collidingObjectHandles: handles of the two colliding objects. This return value is only available when a collision object handle is provided (i.e. explicit handling).
